1. PURPOSE AND HEALTH MANDATE
This policy establishes clinical reporting timelines, medical certificate verification protocols, hospitalization leaves, and psychiatric accommodations for students experiencing acute or chronic medical conditions.

2. REPORTING PROTOCOLS AND TIMELINES
2.1 48-Hour Reporting Rule: Any illness causing student absence for three (3) or more consecutive working days must be reported to the Campus Health Centre and assigned Faculty Advisor within forty-eight (48) hours of symptom onset;
2.2 3-Day Verification Rule: Medical certificates issued by external private hospitals or physicians must be presented in person to the Senior Chief Medical Officer (Health & Wellness Pavilion) within three (3) working days of resuming campus attendance;
2.3 University Medical Verification Slip: Following clinical review, the Chief Medical Officer issues an official University Medical Verification Slip with a unique endorsement code;
2.4 Prolonged Illness and Semester Break: If severe illness exceeds twenty (20) instructional working days, the student may petition the Dean of Academic Affairs for a formal medical semester break (leave of absence) without academic penalty.

3. PENALTIES FOR FRAUDULENT CERTIFICATION
Fabricating, altering, or purchasing fraudulent medical certificates constitutes severe academic dishonesty. Offenders face immediate semester suspension and referral to the Disciplinary Committee.
